    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d687">

                <pb facs="0616" n="540" xml:id="pg540"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/18058</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Special Representative Rodgers
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 6, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>69. Department informed Generals Scott and Obregon have reached satisfactory
                    agreement and that result of their conference has been referred to General
                    Carranza for his approval which, according to General Obregon, is still being
                    awaited.</p>
                <p>Discreetly ascertain and telegraph General Carranza’s attitude in matter soon as
                    possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
